don't  but i'm just saying that having that  malleability and that freedom always  makes episodic a little bit of a  safer way to go  lower risk  but that doesn't make it  lazier that doesn't make it lesser  good episodic television  is still worth seeing and it's worth  pointing out that at this point  very few things are the pure episodic  that things like  law and order or you know 90s 80s and  earlier style sitcoms were  they're still  mostly the hybrids especially if they're  anything even close to dramatic but at  this point  even sitcoms have started getting  overarching stories  so  serialization  can be amazing when it works  but it can go badly and it depends on  sticking the landing so much  just please don't use it as a blanket  defense for the way something's  structured well it's serialized or this  presumption that oh if it's serialized  that'll be better not  necessarily  so yeah i did end up keep circling back  to the doctor who think yeah that's  stuck in my crawl a little bit you know  what we'll wrap it up there though  serialized episodic do you have an  inherent favorite or what are your  favorite  extremely episodic or extremely  serialized shows  whatever your thoughts are drop  something down the comments let's talk  about it  like share subscribe i got a patreon  that's how i pay my bills every little  bit is able to help me out immensely but  even if you can't  don't worry too much about it  because at the end of the day  you are the council i'm just running the  meeting so until next time this council  is adjourned  [Music]  hey if you're sticking around through  the credits might as well hear some  names read out my patreon helps support  this and in particular i want to thank  raven mcbain bookworm mj tracy scrabbit  vincent paul bartolucci kailyn schwartz  edelen robin moore ross schultz shayla  gourlay want to hear me mispronounce  your name check out the rewards on the  patreon  [Music]  [Applause]  [Music]  [Music]  um  [Music]
 

